Notice: the longest bounding box side length of [2.664e+06] is greater than 50.
ElmerGUI includes a library of material properties, defined in SI units.  If using ElmerGUI, 
then the geometry is expected to have meters as length.  Geometry that exceeds 50 meters 
in length or width or height may not be intended.  Many Geometry generators assume 
millimeters as the basic unit of length.  Scaling the geometry from millimeters to meters 
may be the desired action.  For more help, search the Elmer users forum for posts 
about SI units, or for posts about Coordinate Scaling.
Scaling can be accomplished in at least three ways, as follows:
 1. Define the original geometry in meters, not millimeters.
 2. Call ElmerGrid with -scale 0.001 0.001 0.001 as an option.
 3. Add Coordinate Scaling = 0.001 to the simulation section of the sif file.
If using Elmer to analyze large geometry, such as a glacier, then ignore this notice.

